  "Description":          "Audio Scene Management (the author, 2026/10/04: \"ASE is ASM\"). Audio Scene Editing executes every User Command: it opens or creates Basic Audio Objects and Audio Objects, edits them and composes Objects, composes Basic Audio Scenes and Audio Scenes and sets their User Point of View; every edit is a new version in the Module's Shared Storage, from which Objects and Scenes are opened by their identifiers. Capture, reading the User's stored Objects, and hearing the Objects and Scenes - rendered from the User Point of View, and played - are the User Agent's, through the Units of its Physical Layer: the Module takes the Basic Audio Object the User Agent gives and gives back the open Object and the open Scene. Undo, save and stop stay in the User Agent. Speech Translation (the author, 2026/10/03): a User Command naming Translated Objects has a Speech Object translated by Text and Speech Translation into the language its Speech Qualifier states; the translation replaces the original in Shared Storage, under its identifier, so every Scene holding it holds the translation, at its place.",

